From 2c049d69d0683cb47458cd311b2eb8c54589e893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): a stock-source pocket clears the stock around the
 setup's parts

A 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive or 2D Offset with the stock as its source
built the region from the whole stock footprint. The cut went through
the setup's parts, and generate said ok. Only the keep law (#1603)
found the gouge afterwards.

collect_job now builds the region of a stock-source pocket family op
as the stock footprint minus the parts that stand in its step-down
ladder (area::stock_pocket, the same island law as the whole-model
pocket of #12). When no part stands in the ladder, the region is the
stock footprint as before, so no golden changes. When the parts fill
the whole stock outline, generate refuses with a clear message.

An area offset into the part still gouges, and the keep law still
refuses the post. The second finding of the issue (a narrow outside
band skipped with no note) moves to #1655.

Fixes #1554

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
